course: dictionary
lesson: 4541
title: Heartbreak and what it tells us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Heartbreak is a noun that means very great sadness. It often comes when someone you love leaves you or dies, or when you lose something that matters a lot. It can also name the event that causes that sadness.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. In Auntie Bev's Leeds shop, the magazine headline «SOAP STAR'S SECRET HEARTBREAK!» shows a shocking, sad piece of news about a famous person. The presenter giggles about a singer's «secret heartbreak», so it is something private that hurts. Heartbreak is not about a real heart breaking, even though the word is made from heart and break.
explain: Look for clue words near heartbreak, such as losing, leaves, dies or last-minute. Then swap in the meaning «very great sadness» to check it makes sense. Usually you say heartbreak on its own, as in «great heartbreak», and you only say a heartbreak when you mean one sad event.
fact: Heartbreak means very great sadness, often when you lose someone or something you love.
fact: «Heartbreak» is made from heart and break, but it does not mean a real heart breaking.
fact: «Last-minute heartbreak» means a sad moment right at the end, such as a team losing in the final seconds.
fact: «Heartbreak hotel» is the title of a famous song, and it shows how a story can be built around sadness.
fact: As a noun, heartbreak is usually uncountable: you say «great heartbreak», but you say «a heartbreak» only for one sad event.
exercise: «SOAP STAR'S SECRET HEARTBREAK!» is a magazine headline. What does heartbreak mean here? | A kind of cake | *Very great sadness | A happy wedding | A pain in the chest
exercise: Which phrase describes a team losing in the final seconds of a match? | Sunny afternoon picnic | Cheerful cheering | Early-morning breakfast | *Last-minute heartbreak
exercise: Is heartbreak a real heart breaking inside your body? | Yes, but only in winter | No, it is a type of bird | Yes, it always means that | *No, it names a feeling of great sadness
test: Which sentence uses heartbreak to mean an event that causes great sadness? | He drew a heartbreak picture of a cloud | The heartbreak was a blue kind of bird | The bakery had a heartbreak sale on bread | *Losing her dog was a heartbreak for the whole family
test: The fans felt ___ after their team lost in the last minute. | Hiccups | Snow | Holidays | *Heartbreak
exam: What does «Her heartbreak was huge when her best friend moved to Spain» tell us? | *She was very sad because she lost her close friend | Her heart hurt in a physical way | She was very angry with the Spanish | She was very hungry for dinner
